Original commit body from 181d6d934932a3d5e9a83d572c0d983cf39ffbc2:

An unparseable function_summaries.d file crashed verify-claims with
"internal error" and exit 1, the code verify-claims uses for violated:
load_function_summaries parsed with no handling. A live survey of every
catalogue channel found the same defect in more places:

- I/O overlays (--io-primitives, claims extra_catalogs, config.toml,
  io_primitives.d, .hypergumbo.toml): a syntax error crashed in the
  provenance pre-read (overlay_declares_community), before the load that
  would have refused it; a wrong-typed section (net_send: 5) was skipped in
  silence; a repeated key escaped as DuplicateYamlKeyError.
- function_summaries.d: wrong shape skipped in silence, wrong field type
  crashed; under --no-default-overlays the summary split used the taint
  reader and called the file a taint catalog.
- frameworks.d: crashed survey and sketch with exit 1.
- library_signatures.d: py.py reads it at import, so registry discovery
  swallowed the error and the python analyzer vanished (survey exit 0); in
  the analyzer pool the fail-open handler hid it the same way.
- dataflow_patterns.d: a syntax error was skipped in silence.
- sketch swallowed any exception from its cold-cache analysis, so all of
  the above gave a sketch of no analysis at exit 0.

Fix: yaml_catalogs.CatalogueError is the one base type (TaintCatalogError,
IoPrimitiveOverlayError, DuplicateYamlKeyError, DefaultOverlayError derive
from it; the summary, framework, library-signature and dataflow loaders
raise it), read_catalogue_yaml is the shared parse-and-shape check, and
cli.main maps CatalogueError to "Error: <message>" exit 2 at the same
chokepoint as SubstrateError. Analyzer discovery, the analyzer pool and the
sketch auto-run re-raise it instead of containing it. verify-claims reads
the function summaries with the rest of the taint model, so a broken file
is refused there even when no language has both a source and a sink.
IoBoundaryCatalog._from_dict refuses a non-list section or non-mapping row.

Live: 15 verify-claims channels x {syntax, shape, field} with and without
--no-default-overlays, io-boundaries x 4 overlay channels, and survey/sketch
x 3 analysis channels all exit 2 with the file named.

Filed separately: the results cache is not keyed on the user's
analysis-stage channels, so a cached sketch never sees a changed or broken
frameworks.d file (INV-horob-sotir-vijut-bibur-rilob-butun-litad-jijuk).

